<Project>
  <!--
    Shared build settings for the Erewhon strangler projects. Only the component
    Directory.Build.props files under contracts/, standin/, harness/ and facade/ import this file,
    each with the single line
      <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../Erewhon.Strangler.props" />

    No Directory.Build.props or global.json exists at the repository root, on purpose:
    - MSBuild would import a root Directory.Build.props into the existing
      Erewhon/ErewhonDotNetShop projects (ShopUI, ErewhonExposures), and the central package
      management enabled below would then fail their restore with NU1008 against
      ErewhonExposures.csproj's floating Version="22.0.03.*".
    - A root global.json would force this SDK pin on anyone building ErewhonDotNetApp.sln.
    That project floats its package version and has no lock file. These projects do the opposite:
    exact runtime pin, central versions, transitive pinning and committed lock files.

    Contract for the importing projects (not enforced here):
    - A .csproj sets neither TargetFramework nor a Version on any PackageReference. Versions come
      only from the root Directory.Packages.props, which NuGet finds by walking up from the project.
    - Each project commits the packages.lock.json that restore writes. Locked-mode restore is
      requested on the command line by the three Dockerfiles, and by facade/tests/run-tests.sh
      on a fresh checkout that has not been restored yet. harness/scripts/run-local.sh restores
      implicitly and unlocked through dotnet build, so a local build can still regenerate a lock
      file after a deliberate version change.
    - Every dotnet command runs with its working directory inside facade/, standin/ or harness/,
      because dotnet finds the component global.json (SDK 10.0.403, Microsoft.Testing.Platform
      runner) from the working directory, not from the project path.

    The 10.0 pins move only together with the three component global.json files,
    Directory.Packages.props and the three Dockerfiles, and the lock files are then regenerated.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RuntimeFrameworkVersion>10.0.14</RuntimeFrameworkVersion>
    <RollForward>Disable</RollForward>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>true</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>
    <RestorePackagesWithLockFile>true</RestorePackagesWithLockFile>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
